<title>ITALY: Fiat auto division to work Saturdays.</title>
<headline>Fiat auto division to work Saturdays.</headline>
<dateline>TURIN 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fiat's auto division is to work eight Saturday shifts to meet a surge in demand following the introduction of a government car-purchase incentive scheme, a spokesman for the company said.</p>
<p>The spokesman said the Mirafiori works in Turin would work Saturdays on February 8,15, 22, March 1, 8, 15 and 22 and April 12. The factory produces the Panda, Punto and Marea models.</p>
<p>The Termine Marese plant in Sicily, which makes the Punto, would also work Saturday shifts on the same dates.</p>
<p>Fiat's Sevel plant in Val di Sangro, in southern Italy, which manufactures the Ducato van, would work six Saturday shifts.</p>
<p>Fiat has already estimated that January Italian car orders are up 35 percent due to the government bonus scheme.</p>
